\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Surface fit for $F^*(\epsilon ^*,P^*)$. Solid lines are from our model. Dashed lines from Festo supplied data. In total, 537 data points were collected and used to fit the 3D surfaces (321 data points for $\phi $\qty {10}{\mm } BPAs and 216 data points for $\phi $\qty {20}{\mm } BPAs). In total, 80\% of these data were used for training, and 20\% were used for validation. For figure clarity, not all data is included and plotted circles represent collected data at $\pm \qty {10}{\kPa }$ of the stated pressure. (\textbf  {a}) Fit data for $\phi $\qty {10}{\mm } Festo BPAs. (\textbf  {b}) Fit data for $\phi $\qty {20}{\mm } Festo BPAs.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:GenForceFit}{{4}{8}{Surface fit for $F^*(\epsilon ^*,P^*)$. Solid lines are from our model. Dashed lines from Festo supplied data. In total, 537 data points were collected and used to fit the 3D surfaces (321 data points for $\phi $\qty {10}{\mm } BPAs and 216 data points for $\phi $\qty {20}{\mm } BPAs). In total, 80\% of these data were used for training, and 20\% were used for validation. For figure clarity, not all data is included and plotted circles represent collected data at $\pm \qty {10}{\kPa }$ of the stated pressure. (\textbf {a}) Fit data for $\phi $\qty {10}{\mm } Festo BPAs. (\textbf {b}) Fit data for $\phi $\qty {20}{\mm } Festo BPAs.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
